WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.140
If your prep is SuTab, this video will walk you through exactly how to take it

2
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:04.160
.

3
00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.480
Just follow along step by step.

4
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.300
Your SuTab kit includes two bottles of 12 tablets each and a measured

5
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:11.440
container.

6
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.440
Start your first dose between 6 and 7 p.m. the night before your procedure.

7
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.440
Open your first bottle of 12 tablets.

8
00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:24.160
Fill the provided container with 16 ounces of water up to the fill line.

9
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:29.480
Swallow one tablet every two minutes with a sip of water, finishing all 12

10
00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.280
tablets over about 15 to 20 minutes.

11
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.920
Take your time and go at a steady pace.

12
00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.920
About one hour after your last tablet, fill the container again with 16 ounces

13
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:42.280
of water and drink the entire amount slowly over 30 minutes.

14
00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:46.720
Then about 30 minutes after finishing that container, fill it one more time

15
00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:50.720
with 16 ounces of water and drink the entire amount over 30 minutes.

16
00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:52.800
That completes your first dose.

17
00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.810
Repeat the exact same three steps using your second bottle of 12 tablets, one

18
00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:02.950
tablet every two minutes with water, then 16 ounces of water, one hour later,

19
00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:06.840
then 16 ounces of water, 30 minutes after that.

20
00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.910
This part is really important. You must drink all of the prep solution as

21
00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:14.360
directed, even if you're already passing clear liquid.

22
00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:18.670
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us

23
00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:21.360
the clearest view during your procedure.

24
00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:26.030
If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to reschedule and neither

25
00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:26.960
of us wants that.

26
00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:31.840
Between doses, keep drinking clear liquids to stay hydrated. It will help you

27
00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:33.680
feel better and help the prep do its job.

28
00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.700
Do not drink anything at all within four hours of your procedure, including

29
00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:41.160
water, unless it is a small sip to take a medication.

30
00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:45.320
Your procedure may be canceled or rescheduled if this is not followed.

31
00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.120
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom, applying

32
00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:53.880
a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

33
00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:59.670
That's it. You've got this. Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay

34
00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:04.290
hydrated. If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office.

35
00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.680
We're here to help.
